{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1349952-clarity-question","id":1349952,"title":"Clarity Question","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Changeling: The Lost"],"posts":[{"date":"2019-11-20T17:37:16-08:00","id":1349952,"title":"Clarity Question","content":"Hello everyone. <br /> <br /> My apologies is this has already been addressed before.<br /> <br /> Clarity damage is based on Wyrd. And an attached touchstone reduces Clarity damage by one die. So does that mean that a Wyrd 1 changeling with an attached touchstone (or Wyrd 2 changeling with multiple touchstones) never takes mild damage from Breaking Points? Can Clarity damage dice really be reduced to zero? Can\u2019t find this covered in the core book. <br /> <br /> I\u2019m aware that certain conditions and supernatural powers can directly cause Clarity damage or add dice to Clarity damage rolls, but this still feels strange to me. A player brought this to my attention; it seems as though very low-Wyrd changelings don\u2019t generally have to worry much about Breaking Points.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":25750,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25750-holy-hell-thats-hot","user":"Holy-Hell-Thats-Hot","date":". 11-20-2019, 08:47 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25750-holy-hell-thats-hot","name":"Holy-Hell-Thats-Hot","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"31"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-20T17:59:01-08:00","id":1349958,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Holy-Hell-Thats-Hot</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1349952-clarity-question#post1349952\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hello everyone.<br /> <br /> My apologies is this has already been addressed before.<br /> <br /> Clarity damage is based on Wyrd. And an attached touchstone reduces Clarity damage by one die. So does that mean that a Wyrd 1 changeling with an attached touchstone (or Wyrd 2 changeling with multiple touchstones) never takes mild damage from Breaking Points? Can Clarity damage dice really be reduced to zero? Can\u2019t find this covered in the core book.<br /> <br /> I\u2019m aware that certain conditions and supernatural powers can directly cause Clarity damage or add dice to Clarity damage rolls, but this still feels strange to me. A player brought this to my attention; it seems as though very low-Wyrd changelings don\u2019t generally have to worry much about Breaking Points.</div> </div> </div> </div>See the section on The Chance Die on page 176.<br /> <br /> (And yes, characters whose Clarity track can top out as low as <i>2</i> are going to take Clarity damage far less frequently than they roll for breaking points. Much like starting Vampire characters being able to run around without a Clan Bane and minimal damage from short exposure to sunlight, this is working as intended; the number of things that prompt a breaking point only go up over time.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-20T18:13:39-08:00","id":1349962,"title":"","content":"Thank you, Satchel.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25750-holy-hell-thats-hot","name":"Holy-Hell-Thats-Hot","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"31"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}